                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Helps cover eligible travel-related risks and expenses.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>May help manage emergency medical expenses during travel.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>May provide coverage for specified trip cancellation, interruption, or delay.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>May cover baggage loss or other eligible travel-related events.</span></li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Travel Insurance can help reduce the financial impact of unexpected events during domestic or international travel. Coverage, exclusions, premium, claim conditions, geographical limits, and applicable benefits depend on the selected policy and its terms.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Before selecting Travel Insurance, review your destination, travel period, coverage requirements, medical coverage, exclusions, premium, geographical limits, and claim conditions to understand the policy properly.
